---
import readback from "../../example/readback.json";

const ask = readback.marks.find((mark) => mark.role === "ask");
const stop = readback.marks.find((mark) => mark.role === "stop");
const crux = readback.marks.find((mark) => mark.role === "crux");
---

<section class="worked-example" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="example-title">
  <div class="example-intro">
    <h2 id="example-title">Same terrain. A clearer next step.</h2>
    <p>The marked page comes back as a photo. The agent answers the question you marked first, keeps the unresolved choice open, and offers one next page.</p>
    <p class="sitting-detail">A five-page sitting, about 30 minutes, on A4 or Letter paper.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="example-return">
    <figure class="example-photo">
      <div class="photo-frame">
        <div class="marked-paper">
          <img src="/example/generated-page.png" width="1588" height="2246" loading="lazy" alt="Renderer-printed page W1-P2, with Ask, Stop and Crux marks supplied as illustrative text on top." />
          <div class="paper-mark paper-ask"><b>{ask?.mark}</b><span>{ask?.text}</span><small>{ask?.label}</small></div>
          <div class="paper-mark paper-stop"><span>{stop?.text}</span><small>{stop?.label}</small></div>
          <div class="paper-mark paper-crux"><span>{crux?.text}</span><small>{crux?.label}</small></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>Illustrative example · W1-P2 · photographed return with authored marks</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="example-readback">
      <h3>Agent reads it back</h3>
      <div class="reply-row"><h4>Q1, answered first</h4><p>{readback.answerFirst}</p></div>
      <div class="reply-row"><h4>Stop, carried forward</h4><p>{readback.unresolved}</p></div>
      <div class="reply-row"><h4>Next move</h4><p>{readback.nextMove}</p></div>
      <p class="readback-uncertainty">{readback.uncertainty}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="example-next">
    <div class="next-copy">
      <h3>The next page</h3>
      <p>One page for the open choice. Sort the ideas from W1-P2 into what belongs in v1, what waits, and what goes out.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="next-paper">
      <img src="/example/next-page.png" width="1588" height="2246" loading="lazy" alt="Real Switchback renderer output W2-P1, a blank write-in card sort for what v1 says no to." />
      <figcaption>Illustrative example · W2-P1 · the next round as printed</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
